{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2170-04-11 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of your hospital doctors. You're here because your legs have been swelling more than usual?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2170-04-11 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, they’ve gotten so big and painful. I’ve gained over 20 pounds in a few weeks. My legs are tight, they blister, and when I lie down, the swelling goes into my belly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2170-04-11 18:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you’ve been taking your diuretics, the water pills, like usual?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2170-04-11 18:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, every day. I’m also on salt and fluid limits. Nothing’s helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2170-04-11 18:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. We’ll start IV diuretics to help pull off the extra fluid. We’ll monitor your labs closely. Your heart function will be checked with an echo."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2170-04-11 18:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that help me breathe better? I get short of breath just walking to the bathroom."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2170-04-11 18:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, reducing the fluid should help. The chest X-ray shows no fluid in your lungs now, so that’s good. But your legs are holding a lot of fluid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2170-04-11 18:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I also had chills the last couple days. Could I be fighting an infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2170-04-11 18:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your urine and it’s clean. No fever now, and no signs of cellulitis. We’ll keep you on doxycycline as a preventive since you’ve had it before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2170-04-11 18:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2170-04-12 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We’re going to place a PICC line so we can give your IV diuretics safely over the next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2170-04-12 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safe? I had a blood clot in my arm before from a PICC."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2170-04-12 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand your concern. We’ll place it on the right side and confirm the position with an X-ray. We’ll also keep your warfarin going to prevent clots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2170-04-12 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The PICC is in, but the tip was too high. We’ll reposition it later today under X-ray guidance to make sure it’s in the right spot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2170-04-12 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2170-04-12 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get some numbing medicine. It’s a quick procedure, and you’ll be awake. Most patients tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2170-04-12 17:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The PICC is now correctly placed in the large vein near your heart. We’ve started the IV lasix."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2170-04-12 17:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I already feel a little less pressure in my legs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2170-04-13 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your echo came back. Your heart is pumping well, so this swelling isn’t from heart failure. It’s likely lymphedema or venous stasis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2170-04-13 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So why am I so swollen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2170-04-13 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your body isn’t draining fluid properly, and with your weight, the veins and lymph system are under strain. The IV diuretics will help reduce the load."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2170-04-13 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I see. My weight hasn’t gone down much though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2170-04-13 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common. The scale might not reflect changes if fluid shifts. But your legs do look smaller. We’re tracking your intake and output too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2170-04-14 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs show your white count is still high, but no infection signs. We’ll keep the doxycycline as a preventive."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2170-04-14 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that from stress or inflammation?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2170-04-14 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Likely. Your body is under strain from the fluid overload. It’s not an infection, so we won’t add antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2170-04-15 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR was low yesterday. We’ve increased your warfarin dose to 8 mg daily to get it back in range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2170-04-15 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on warfarin for years. Why is it fluctuating now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2170-04-15 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Illness, diet changes, or other meds can affect it. We’ll monitor closely and adjust as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2170-04-16 22:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m told you had a seizure last night?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2170-04-16 22:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t remember it. The nurse said I was twitching and frothing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2170-04-16 22:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It looked like a generalized seizure. Your levetiracetam level was normal, but we think fluid overload may have triggered it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2170-04-16 22:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But my level was okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2170-04-16 22:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but sometimes even therapeutic levels aren’t enough during stress. We’re increasing your dose to 1500 mg twice daily to be safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2170-04-16 22:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll take it as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2170-04-17 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine went up slightly, so we’re stopping the IV lasix. We don’t want to hurt your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2170-04-17 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the swelling might come back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2170-04-17 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll switch to a higher dose of oral bumetanide—4 mg daily. You’ll also go to the diuretic clinic for occasional IV treatments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2170-04-17 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was worried about peeing all the time. Is 4 mg once a day okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2170-04-17 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start with once daily to see how you tolerate it. We can adjust if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2170-04-18 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your A1c came back at 6.4, which suggests prediabetes. We’ll monitor your sugars and encourage diet changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2170-04-18 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve always had borderline sugars. Should I see an endocrinologist?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2170-04-18 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. Your PCP can follow this. Focus on low-sugar choices and monitoring weight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2170-04-19 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your legs are still swollen, but less tender. The papules on your skin aren’t infected. We’ll keep the antifungal cream for itching."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2170-04-19 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The canker sores on my tongue are bothering me. Any advice?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2170-04-19 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’re common with stress or vitamin changes. Rinse with warm salt water. They should heal in a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2170-04-20 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re planning discharge in a couple days. Your INR is now 2.0, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2170-04-20 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. I want to get home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2170-04-21 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve scheduled follow-up with your PCP to check your levetiracetam level and INR. Call if your weight goes up more than 3 pounds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2170-04-21 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the diuretic clinic?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2170-04-21 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’ll contact you to reschedule. You may need IV diuretics every few weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2170-04-22 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your discharge weight is 156.1 kg. It hasn’t changed much, but your legs look better. The scale might not capture fluid shifts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2170-04-22 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I feel lighter."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2170-04-23 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re discharging tomorrow. You’ll go home with increased levetiracetam, warfarin, and bumetanide."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2170-04-23 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the pain meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2170-04-23 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, keep using oxycontin and morphine as needed. Also, we added stool softeners to prevent constipation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2170-04-24 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final labs look stable. Your potassium is good, and white count is still mildly high but not concerning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2170-04-24 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the swelling might come back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2170-04-24 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It might. That’s why we’re setting up the diuretic clinic and close follow-up. Watch your weight and symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2170-04-25 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home tomorrow. A nurse will call with instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2170-04-25 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2170-04-25 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2170-04-26 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We’ll get you discharged by noon. Your final meds are ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2170-04-26 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2170-04-26 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Remember: weigh daily, take your meds, and follow up with your PCP and neurology."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2170-04-26 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And the diuretic clinic?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2170-04-26 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’ll call you. If swelling worsens before then, come back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2170-04-26 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2170-04-26 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2170-04-26 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The transport team will take you to the lobby in 30 minutes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2170-04-26 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m all packed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2170-04-26 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your warfarin is now 8 mg daily. Check your INR at the lab next week and fax it to your doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2170-04-26 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2170-04-26 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And keep taking the levetiracetam twice a day. Neurology will see you in two months."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2170-04-26 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I have the appointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2170-04-26 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. You’re all set."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2170-04-26 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just confirming—I take the bumetanide once a day, not twice?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2170-04-26 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Correct. We lowered it to once daily to reduce frequent urination. Call if swelling returns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2170-04-26 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2170-04-26 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Stay well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2170-04-26 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your ride is here. Here’s your discharge summary."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2170-04-26 11:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2170-04-26 11:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2170-04-26 11:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2170-04-26 11:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2170-04-11 17:56:00",
    "admission_end": "2170-04-26 14:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 58-year-old woman was admitted for acute on chronic lower extremity edema worsened over several weeks, unresponsive to oral diuretics. She was started on IV furosemide via a PICC line after initial placement and repositioning confirmed by imaging. Echocardiogram showed preserved systolic function, supporting lymphedema or venous stasis as the cause. The hospital course was complicated by a generalized seizure, likely triggered by volume overload, prompting an increase in levetiracetam dose despite therapeutic levels. IV diuresis was stopped due to a slight rise in creatinine, and she was transitioned to higher-dose oral bumetanide. Her warfarin was uptitrated to achieve a therapeutic INR. Leukocytosis persisted without infection. She was discharged home with increased diuretic and seizure medication, instructions for weight monitoring, and follow-up in primary care, neurology, and an outpatient diuretic clinic.",
    "problems": [
      "Other lymphedema",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Body Mass Index 50.0-59.9, adult",
      "Other fluid overload",
      "Morbid obesity",
      "Epilepsy, unspecified, without mention of intractable epilepsy",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism",
      "Leukocytosis, unspecified",
      "Myalgia and myositis, unspecified",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult)(pediatric)",
      "Tobacco use disorder",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of other female genital organs",
      "Unspecified pruritic disorder",
      "Other symbolic dysfunction",
      "Oral aphthae",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage I through stage IV, or unspecified",
      "Chronic kidney disease, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
